  "body": "There are apartments on Tamaki Drive, and then there are residences like this. The kind that rarely come up, and once secured, are held.\r\n\r\n201B sits directly on the waterfront, occupying a two-level penthouse position in a boutique building of just two. Private, quiet, and completely removed from the usual apartment experience.\r\n\r\nInside, the scale is immediate. Approximately 204m² of well-proportioned space, with living unfolding across the upper level where the harbour takes centre stage. The outlook stretches uninterrupted to Rangitoto, with light shifting across the water throughout the day.\r\n\r\nThe layout is deliberate and quietly luxurious. A lower level of two bedrooms and a bathroom creates a natural guest or family zone, while upstairs is reserved for living and retreat. Here, two further bedrooms and two bathrooms – including a master suite of real substance – sit alongside the main living, elevating the entire upper level into something that feels more akin to a private residence than an apartment. A dedicated office completes the picture, seamlessly integrated.\r\n\r\nEverything here speaks to quality. Solid construction, immaculate presentation, and a level of care that’s increasingly hard to find. A swimming pool adds another layer – unexpected in a building of this size, and a reminder that this is something altogether more considered.\r\n\r\nStep outside and Tamaki Drive becomes part of the everyday. Morning swims at Kohimarama Beach, coffee along the waterfront, evenings where the harbour settles and the pace slows.\r\n\r\nThere are plenty of apartments along here.\r\n\r\nVery few like this.\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
